{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01074",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.96,
      "end_seconds": 6.87,
      "duration_seconds": 5.91,
      "text": "All set here, doctor. Chart's updated, and I'll read the readings out when you're ready."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.43,
      "end_seconds": 12.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Perfect, thanks. Hello there, so what's the trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 13.23,
      "end_seconds": 20.21,
      "duration_seconds": 6.98,
      "text": "Hmm, hello, doctor. I hope it's alright if I stay in for this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.76,
      "end_seconds": 24.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Yes, that's no problem at all. Please sit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.74,
      "end_seconds": 31.48,
      "duration_seconds": 5.74,
      "text": "Yeah, it's a blocked nose. I don't know what's causing it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.49,
      "end_seconds": 35.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.32,
      "end_seconds": 51.5,
      "duration_seconds": 11.18,
      "text": "Around two days... no wait, it's more like five days. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.01,
      "end_seconds": 54.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "How strong would you say it is?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.67,
      "end_seconds": 60.79,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "Mm, uh, pretty severe, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.76,
      "end_seconds": 65.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "Any a poor sense of smell as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.09,
      "end_seconds": 78.98,
      "duration_seconds": 11.89,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, yes, about the same, ten days. Um, I had green discharge before. That's settled now, though."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.06,
      "end_seconds": 84.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.81,
      "text": "So, a few quick ones: fever, double vision or severe headache?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.07,
      "end_seconds": 91.19,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "No, no fever, double vision or severe headache."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.84,
      "end_seconds": 95.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "What about swelling around the eye?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.24,
      "end_seconds": 105.26,
      "duration_seconds": 6.02,
      "text": "Um, not that I've noticed, no swelling around the eye."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.31,
      "end_seconds": 111.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.85,
      "end_seconds": 115.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "Nothing unusual, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.21,
      "end_seconds": 127.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "What conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.93,
      "end_seconds": 140.06,
      "duration_seconds": 11.13,
      "text": "I have asthma, for about ten years. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.38,
      "end_seconds": 145.29,
      "duration_seconds": 0.91,
      "text": "Mm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.6,
      "end_seconds": 156.41,
      "duration_seconds": 9.81,
      "text": "Uh, I have acid reflux, for nearly five years. Mm, I've had heart disease, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.97,
      "end_seconds": 169.51,
      "duration_seconds": 12.54,
      "text": "Hm, okay. Yes, asthma and acid reflux are known to us, good to have that clear. Alright, is there anything relevant on the family side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.26,
      "end_seconds": 176.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "My mother had a stroke. My brother has epilepsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.49,
      "end_seconds": 195.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Do you live by yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.58,
      "end_seconds": 200.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.4,
      "end_seconds": 203.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "And your job?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.39,
      "end_seconds": 208.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "I work in accounts at a hospital."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.58,
      "end_seconds": 213.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.62,
      "end_seconds": 220.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "So, uh, no, not that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 221.63,
      "end_seconds": 229.11,
      "duration_seconds": 7.48,
      "text": "Hold on, doctor, I think he reacted to tramadol once. I'm not certain, though."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.75,
      "end_seconds": 234.91,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "Right, um, maybe, but I don't recall it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.95,
      "end_seconds": 246.4,
      "duration_seconds": 8.45,
      "text": "Okay, I'll note both of those. What's on your current medicine list? Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 247.13,
      "end_seconds": 261.22,
      "duration_seconds": 14.09,
      "text": "He takes Asthalin inhaler, when needed. Oh, he takes omeprazole, 20 milligrams, once a day for the reflux. So, it's aspirin, 75 milligrams, once a day, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.72,
      "end_seconds": 271.85,
      "duration_seconds": 6.13,
      "text": "Um, I used to take clopidogrel, but I stopped it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.99,
      "end_seconds": 285.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Anything surgical in your history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 287.77,
      "end_seconds": 294.39,
      "duration_seconds": 6.62,
      "text": "Yes, you know, I had a triple bypass, eight years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 295.66,
      "end_seconds": 304.64,
      "duration_seconds": 8.98,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Respiratory rate 15, pulse 80, pressure 113 over 77, SpO2 97 percent on room air."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.97,
      "end_seconds": 307.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.31,
      "end_seconds": 313.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "Let me look at the area, I'll be gentle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.63,
      "end_seconds": 317.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "Hold that for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.74,
      "end_seconds": 336.37,
      "duration_seconds": 5.63,
      "text": "There is tenderness over both cheeks and the nasal lining looks swollen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 341.46,
      "end_seconds": 353.36,
      "duration_seconds": 11.9,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again. Putting it all together, I think we're dealing with chronic sinusitis at this stage. I'd also keep nasal polyps in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 354.97,
      "end_seconds": 357.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Well, will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 361.63,
      "end_seconds": 386.58,
      "duration_seconds": 24.95,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like chronic sinusitis. The treatment will be mometasone nasal spray, 50 micrograms, two sprays each side once a day, eight weeks. That's for sinus inflammation. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 387.49,
      "end_seconds": 391.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "I, I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 392.95,
      "end_seconds": 394.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "Right, look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}